FUNCTION CALLC.EXISTS(FNAME)
* udt_curses — Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.  GPL-2.0-only.
*
* CALLC.EXISTS(name) — 1 if the CallC function `name` is registered with
* this UniData, else 0, WITHOUT invoking it.  A CallC to an unregistered
* function aborts the whole program, so a live probe is impossible; instead
* this reads the canonical CallC definition that the package installer
* maintains ($UDTHOME/bin/work/cfuncdef).
*
* The point is optional native capability: a program can ask whether an
* add-on like udt_curses is present and light up the better path when it is,
* falling back cleanly when it is not — the same binary runs on a plain
* account and on one where the ncurses bridge is installed.  Ship this with
* the package manager so every installed package can rely on it.
   FOUND = 0
   UDT = GETENV("UDTHOME")
   IF UDT # "" THEN
      OSREAD DEF FROM UDT : "/bin/work/cfuncdef" ELSE DEF = ""
      NL = DCOUNT(DEF, CHAR(10))
      I = 1
      LOOP WHILE I <= NL AND FOUND = 0 DO
         IF FIELD(FIELD(DEF, CHAR(10), I), ":", 1) = FNAME THEN FOUND = 1
         I = I + 1
      REPEAT
   END
   RETURN FOUND
